			(passive) and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέτερα</span> (neuter),
				<i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.59
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VI.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. τόνος</span>
			<i>real</i> or <i>unmodified</i> (cf. supr. <i><span class="en">
				111.3
			</span></i>) accent, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκλινόμενος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				36.10
			</span></i>, al.; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθὴ τάσις</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				54.8
			</span></i>, al. (The gloss of <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βορθ-αγορίσκοι,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ.</span>
			, and the dialect forms of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρθεία</span> (q.v.), suggest that the word orig. had
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ.</span>)</div>
